From 91a7e33f784a9485f4c07db33dcb7924257dfeab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:53:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] feat(cli): error codes in every error line, JSON error
 objects, no transport keys

Agents branch on error codes, but the CLI printed only the message
("Error: Page is not ready: login at ...") while the host had attached
code=page_login. Append the code to the first line of every error
("... [page_login]", the form surf extract already used) and, under
--json, also print {"error": {"code", "message", "details"}} on
stdout so a --json caller never has to parse prose.

Strip the extension message id and _resolved* keys from page.readiness,
wait.ready and frame.diagnose --json output and from extract's readiness
block: they change between runs and mean nothing to the caller.
formatToolContent drops _resolvedWindowId alongside _resolvedTabId.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PpyRJ9kNJBQ5JiqeYjxkTF
